@page "/docs/api-reference/authorize"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Authorize — Vaultex API</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">API reference</div>
<h1>Authorize</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Starts an authorization request. The user is sent to Vaultex's sign-in screen and, after
    authenticating, redirected back to your <code>redirect_uri</code> with an authorization code.
</p>

<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span>
    <span>/connect/authorize</span>
</div>

<h2 id="parameters">Query parameters</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>response_type</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Always <code>code</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client_id</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Identifier of the registered client.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>redirect_uri</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Must exactly match a redirect URI on the client.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Space-separated. Must include <code>openid</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>state</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Opaque value returned unchanged. CSRF protection.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>code_challenge</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Base64URL SHA-256 of the PKCE verifier.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>code_challenge_method</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Always <code>S256</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nonce</code></td><td>string</td><td>Recommended</td><td>Returned in the ID token to prevent replays.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>prompt</code></td><td>string</td><td>Optional</td><td><code>none</code>, <code>login</code>, or <code>consent</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>login_hint</code></td><td>string</td><td>Optional</td><td>Pre-fill the username field.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>max_age</code></td><td>number</td><td>Optional</td><td>Force re-auth if last login was longer ago than this (seconds).</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="example-request">Example request</h2>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">URL</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/authorize?
  response_type=code
  &amp;client_id=your-client-id
  &amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fyourapp.com%2Fcallback
  &amp;scope=openid%20profile%20email
  &amp;state=xyz123
  &amp;code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM
  &amp;code_challenge_method=S256
  &amp;nonce=n-0S6_WzA2Mj</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="example-response">Example success redirect</h2>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">HTTP</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: https://yourapp.com/callback?code=Abc123...&amp;state=xyz123</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="error-response">Error redirect</h2>
<p>If something goes wrong, Vaultex redirects with an <code>error</code> query parameter instead of a code.</p>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">HTTP</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: https://yourapp.com/callback?error=access_denied&amp;error_description=User+cancelled&amp;state=xyz123</code></pre>
</div>

